# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which silently rewrites line
# endings on checkout. These rules pin the endings explicitly so that the same
# commit produces the same working tree on every platform, whatever the local
# Git settings say.

# Text files: normalised to LF in the repository and checked out as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must run on Unix, where a CRLF shebang line is a syntax error.
# Repeated explicitly so detection can never misclassify one.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary fixtures and assets: excluded from all text handling, so no checkout
# or add ever converts them. These are raw bytes — protocol capture frames,
# prop blobs, images, the name-tag font, the app icons and the SoundFont — and
# a line-ending rewrite would corrupt them.
*.bin binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ttf binary
*.sf2 binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
